Maintainer decision 2026-11-06: only release tags publish the OCP image. Pushes to main, feature branches and pull requests build the image and push nothing.

Until now .cicd/docker+29+publish.image.sh publishes on main and on any tag. Every push to main since at least 2026-10-01 (run 36813555940, ac075c6) pushed raudssus/ocp:latest + :<sha> to Docker Hub and ghcr.io/getty/kubernetes-ocp. Most recently: run 41741299801, 44a9db0. ADR 0013 says publishing never runs without explicit permission, and that was not true for main pushes.

Scope:
- Gate in .cicd/docker+29+publish.image.sh: publish only when CICD_TAG is a release tag. Anything else exits 78 (skip). That includes main, other tags such as the existing k138-debug, PRs and branches. Release tag = the [@Author::GETTY] tag_format %v (bare version, e.g. 0.001), which is also the tag robocop of a released CLI pulls (OCP::Robocop::Manifest _default_image: raudssus/ocp:<version>). Limiting it to release-shaped tags is the main agent's call: a debug tag must not move latest.
- Comments that state the old policy: the headers of both .cicd scripts and .github/workflows/ci.yml.
- Prose: docs/development.md (CI, Publish policy), docs/robocop.md (a development checkout falls back to :latest, which is now the newest release, not main), README.md (pin example raudssus/ocp:v0.001 -> 0.001, the bare-version tag the release writes).
- ADR 0013 amendment recording the decision and the history.

Consequence to know: until the first release tag, latest stays at 44a9db0.

Closes k134 together (its open points are met: secrets in place since 2026-09-04, siblings on CPAN since 2026-10-21, a fresh checkout builds without vendor/, CI green on main).

